xtÙ6But mercy and truth shall be to them that devise good.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text¾In all labour there is profit:¦layout ‚¤textÙ0But the talk of the lips tendeth only to penury.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ&The crown of the wise is their riches:¦layout ‚¤textÙ&But the foolishness of fools is folly.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ A true witness delivereth souls:¦layout ‚¤textÙ&But a deceitful witness speaketh lies.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ-In the fear of the LORD is strong confidence:¦layout ‚¤textÙ.And his children shall have a place of refuge.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ+The fear of the LORD is a fountain of life,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#To depart from the snares of death.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ0In the multitude of people is the king's honour:¦layout ‚¤textÙ;But in the want of people is the destruction of the prince.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ3He that is slow to wrath is of great understanding:¦layout ‚¤textÙ.But he that is hasty of spirit exalteth folly.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ'A sound heart is the life of the flesh:¦layout ‚¤textÙ%But envy the rottenness of the bones.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ2He that oppresseth the poor reproacheth his Maker:¦layout ‚¤textÙ1But he that honoureth him hath mercy on the poor.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ,The wicked is driven away in his wickedness:¦layout ‚¤textÙ)But the righteous hath hope in his death.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse …¤book§chapter«first_verse!ªlast_verse#¦verses“„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines’‚¤textÙ;Wisdom resteth in the heart of him that hath understanding:¦layout ‚¤textÙ6But that which is in the midst of fools is made known.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ Righteousness exalteth a nation:¦layout ‚¤textÙ$But sin is a reproach to any people.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤textÙ+The king's favour is toward a wise servant:¦layout ‚¤textÙ0But his wrath is against him that causeth shame.¦layout§quote_2ªlast_verse#